WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.220
Hey everyone, привет, welcome to привет, русский эпизод 26-18 мая 2026 года.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:10.980
I'm Olya, indeed got some great Russian words to learn today.

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:12.880
Поехали, let's go!

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:15.500
Our word of the day is cosmos.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:17.700
Listen closely, cosmos.

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:20.480
Now say it's lolly with me, cosmos.

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:24.540
This word means space, like the universe all around us.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:28.900
It sounds exactly like the English word cosmos, which makes it easy to remember.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:30.800
Let me use it in a sentence.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:33.120
Я вижу звёзды в космосе.

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:35.380
That means I see stars in space.

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:37.760
Now repeat after me, cosmos.

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:41.000
Let's keep building our space vocabulary together.

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:43.280
Our next word is raketa.

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:45.280
Repeat after me, raketa.

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:46.740
This means rocket.

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:51.620
Imagine a rocket racing like a fast rocket in a game, and you will never forget it.

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:53.040
Here is a simple sentence.

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:56.480
Raketa летит в небо, the rocket flies into the sky.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:59.820
Now that you know raketa, let's learn звезда.

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:02.280
Repeat after me, звезда.

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:04.340
This word means star.

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:07.740
Think of звезда, winkling like a dazzling star in the sky.

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:09.180
Try this sentence.

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:11.360
Звезда яркая ночью.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:13.200
The star is bright at night.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:15.480
Next comes planeta.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:17.400
Repeat after me, planeta.

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:18.260
It means planet.

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:21.000
Planet sounds almost the same in English,

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:23.380
so this one is simple to keep in your mind.

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:24.580
Listen to the sentence.

00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:26.600
Земля это planeta.

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:27.740
Earth is a planet.

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:29.440
We have Luna next.

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:30.860
Repeat after me, Luna.

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:32.260
This means moon.

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:35.540
Luna is like the name of the moon in stories and songs.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:37.220
Here is how we use it.

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:38.820
Luna светит ночью.

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:40.360
The moon shines at night.

00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:42.280
Now say, солнце with me.

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:43.440
Repeat after me.

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:44.540
Солнце.

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:46.460
This word means sun.

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:50.520
Picture the sun as a big glowing soul, like solar energy.

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:51.700
And it will stick.

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:53.220
Use it like this.

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:54.540
Солнце теплое.

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:55.560
The sun is warm.

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:57.120
Let's add земля.

00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:58.280
Repeat after me.

00:01:58.660 --> 00:01:59.100
Земля.

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:00.520
This means earth.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:04.080
Земля sounds like them for the ground under your feet.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:05.540
Listen to the sentence.

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:07.320
Мы живем на земле.

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:08.740
We live on earth.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:11.780
Our last vocabulary word is спутник.

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:12.840
Repeat after me.

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:13.700
Спутник.

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:15.100
It means satellite.

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:17.560
The first satellite was called спутник.

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:20.280
And now the word means any satellite in the sky.

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:21.600
Try this sentence.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:23.700
Спутник летает вокруг земли.

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:25.520
The satellite flies around earth.

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:27.620
Now for a quick grammar bite.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:29.720
In Russian, nouns have genders,

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:31.480
like masculine or feminine.

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:34.620
These genders change word endings in sentences.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:38.120
Kosmos is masculine, while Raketa is feminine.

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:41.440
That is why we add certain endings when we describe them.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.100
English does not change endings for gender,

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:47.920
but Russian uses this pattern to make sentences flow nicely.

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:51.800
But these space words, you can already build simple descriptions.

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:54.720
Russians feel proud of their space history.

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:58.880
Yuri Gagarin became the first human in space in 1961.

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:02.940
Families often watch special shows about Kasmanocht's

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:04.700
on Kasmanocht's day each April.

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:07.820
This holiday celebrates how exploring space

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:09.780
brings people together around the world.

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:12.240
It is time for our practice challenge.

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:16.000
For the kids, draw a picture of the sun, moon and the rocket,

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.320
then label each one with the Russian words

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:19.820
while saying them out loud.

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:22.840
For the adults, look up at the night sky tonight,

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:25.180
practice saying Yavizhu Zvizdu,

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:28.420
and Yavizhu Luno to a friend or family member.

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:31.940
Now here is something really cool about one of today's words.

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:34.360
Did you know that the Russian word Kosmos

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:37.940
and the English word Kosmos are actually the same word?

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:41.140
They both come from the ancient Greek word Kosmos,

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:43.160
meaning order and the universe.

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:46.820
This word traveled through Latin into European languages

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:51.600
and reached Russian in the 1800s as scientists studied the stars.

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:55.840
Be careful though, because Sputnik can mean satellite in space,

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:59.120
yet it also simply means companion in everyday Russian.

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:01.020
That creates a fun surprise.

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:03.700
Next time you hear the English word Kosmos,

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:06.980
remember it is Kasmans with the Russian Kosmos.

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:10.500
They share the Greek root for the beautiful order universe.

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:14.740
That connection becomes your secret shortcut to remembering it forever.

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:15.960
Молодец.

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:17.560
That means well done.

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:20.780
Remember, every expert started as a beginner,

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:23.240
practicing today's words out loud,

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:24.300
even just once,

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:26.600
and you'll be amazed how fast you learn.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:27.940
See you next time.

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:29.700
Poka, that's Russian 4x.

